                    "fillColor": "#a3adbd",
                    "fillOpacity": 1
                  }
                ],
                "fontFamily": "Arimo",
                "text": "Four columns follow the active bank; changing view or bank preserves selection and playback. Tracks retains one whole-track meter. Mixer adds stereo meters, independent Mute and multi-track Solo, pan, and a gain marker. Touch and encoder edits stay local until committed; changing selection, opening another editor or replacing the session cancels the old draft. Double-tap restores the default without committing an intermediate value."
              }
            ],
            "textTransform": "none",
            "textAlign": "left",
            "fontId": "custom-99a2c890-1804-450c-8af8-6b60ee9a6b27",
            "fontSize": "28",
            "fontWeight": "400",
            "type": "paragraph",
            "fontVariantId": "normal-400",
            "textDecoration": "none",
            "letterSpacing": "0",
            "fills": [
              {
                "fillColor": "#a3adbd",
                "fillOpacity": 1
              }
            ],
            "fontFamily": "Arimo"
          },
          {
            "lineHeight": "1.4",
            "fontStyle": "normal",
            "children": [
              {
                "lineHeight": "1.4",
                "fontStyle": "normal",
                "textTransform": "none",
                "fontId": "custom-99a2c890-1804-450c-8af8-6b60ee9a6b27",
                "fontSize": "28",
                "fontWeight": "400",
                "fontVariantId": "normal-400",
                "textDecoration": "none",
                "letterSpacing": "0",
                "fills": [
                  {
                    "fillColor": "#a3adbd",
                    "fillOpacity": 1
                  }
                ],
                "fontFamily": "Arimo",
                "text": "Mixer gain spans silence to +6 dB on its own logarithmic axis; side dBFS scales describe measured signal, not gain. Reset asks first, then restores all eight levels and pans, preserving mute, Solo, FX, routes and audio history. Compact windows retain four readable strips."
              }
            ],
            "textTransform": "none",
            "textAlign": "left",
            "fontId": "custom-99a2c890-1804-450c-8af8-6b60ee9a6b27",
            "fontSize": "28",
            "fontWeight": "400",
            "type": "paragraph",
            "fontVariantId": "normal-400",
            "textDecoration": "none",
            "letterSpacing": "0",
            "fills": [
              {
                "fillColor": "#a3adbd",
                "fillOpacity": 1
              }
            ],
            "fontFamily": "Arimo"
          },
          {
            "lineHeight": "1.4",
            "fontStyle": "normal",
            "children": [
              {
                "lineHeight": "1.4",
                "fontStyle": "normal",
                "textTransform": "none",
                "fontId": "custom-99a2c890-1804-450c-8af8-6b60ee9a6b27",
                "fontSize": "28",
                "fontWeight": "400",
                "fontVariantId": "normal-400",
                "textDecoration": "none",
                "letterSpacing": "0",
                "fills": [
                  {
                    "fillColor": "#a3adbd",
                    "fillOpacity": 1
                  }
                ],
                "fontFamily": "Arimo",
                "text": "FX bypass uses the existing chain; direct FX editing arrives with slice 3f. Backing\/click strips and foot performance use their later shared owners. No invented CPU telemetry or touch lock; these retain their separate implementation work. Recording indication remains beside Library. Bars show \u2014 until a tempo grid counts them."
              }
            ],
            "textTransform": "none",
            "textAlign": "left",
            "fontId": "custom-99a2c890-1804-450c-8af8-6b60ee9a6b27",
